Expressive therapy is based on using the creative arts to help people heal. There's art therapy, music therapy, writing therapy. I'm sure you can see where I'm going with this.

228
02:11:57,939 --> 02:12:04,939
Well, today we're going to talk about dance therapy and how it is used to treat both physical and mental illnesses.

229
02:12:04,939 --> 02:12:18,939
First, dance therapy helps the body. It does this by providing a form of physical exercise. Dance in and of itself is an excellent form of exercise. It requires the use of many different muscle groups.

230
02:12:18,939 --> 02:12:24,939
The result is that a person finds it easier to move around and has better muscle coordination.

231
02:12:24,939 --> 02:12:35,939
It also has been found to help with respiration and circulation. Additionally, many patients feel better after dance therapy since it reduces physical tension in the muscles.

232
02:12:35,939 --> 02:12:42,939
Second, it has been shown to be very effective when used with patients suffering from mental illnesses.

233
02:12:42,939 --> 02:12:53,939
This is because dance therapy allows people both creative and emotional release. Many people who are mentally ill do not express themselves because they are afraid they will be misunderstood.

234
02:12:53,939 --> 02:13:08,939
Through dance therapy, they are able to get their emotions out through movement. Dance therapy also helps patients build confidence and self-esteem. Since they are able to independently create their own performances, they feel proud of themselves.

